  "status_text": "Eight doors shut on one search between 17:16 and 19:37 UTC. The question: is there a five-dimensional space of 4 by 5 grids of complex numbers in which every row and every column sums to zero and three sums built from the grid's smaller permanents all vanish? The largest space known has dimension four, and the search is still open (L-gct-199, a conjecture). This evening eight restrictions on what such a space could look like were checked in Lean, four of them by proofs from outside contributors (L-gct-280, 282, 284, 286; and 289, 290, 291, 292). The unrestricted case is open.",
